{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792313919,"nonce":"fpgjRbclW3eLHtXDNbQcaS1aVK4=","title":"Terminal tab: an embedded system shell","message":"The user wants a Terminal tab like VS Code's, beside Problems and Output: the user's own shell (zsh, bash, PowerShell) running in the project folder, interactive, with several terminals, new, split, kill and rename.\n\nA native terminal app cannot be embedded: macOS and Wayland do not let one process re-parent another's window, and it would not follow the theme. So RayDE runs the shell itself and draws it, in three parts.\n\n1. A pseudo-terminal. A shell must see a tty (prompts, colours, line editing, vim, ssh), which pipes from sys.io.Process do not give. Rust, as native/image is: a native library (hdll) over the portable-pty crate (macOS and Linux openpty/forkpty, Windows ConPTY): open(cols, rows, shell, cwd, env), write(bytes), resize, a non-blocking read, exit status, kill. TERM=xterm-256color, COLORTERM=truecolor.\n2. A terminal emulator, in the same library: alacritty_terminal (Apache-2.0) or wezterm-term keeps the cell grid, colours, cursor, scrollback, the alternate screen, mouse reporting and bracketed paste. The grid stays in Rust; Haxe asks each frame for the rows that changed (text runs with colours and attributes), never a Haxe object per cell. Rust owns the memory and drops a session's arenas when it closes.\n3. A view. ashui gets a TerminalView component (not RayDE: ChimpMonk's editor wants it too): draws the grid on a canvas from the changed rows, sizes cols and rows from its box and the font's cell, maps keys and modifiers to bytes (arrows, function keys, Ctrl-keys, Option as Meta, paste), selection and copy, a scrollbar over the scrollback, links, IME. It takes a source interface (rows, cursor, input, resize), so it does not depend on the PTY library.\n\nRayDE then adds: the Terminal tab in the bottom panel with a toolbar as VS Code's (new terminal, shell profile menu, split, kill, rename, maximise), a list of terminals when there are several, the shell chosen from $SHELL and /etc/shells, terminals kept running while the panel is hidden, and the project's runtime on PATH (ash, haxe). Open questions: whether Run could print to a terminal instead of Output (it would then handle input); shell integration (command marks, cwd tracking) later.\n\nOrder: the native library with a Haxe test that runs `echo` and reads the grid; TerminalView in ashui against a fake source; the tab. Needs ashui's CodeEditor font metrics for the cell size, and canvas draw of many text runs cheaply (see 3bb2f66's lessons on per-frame element churn: one canvas, no element a cell).","files":null}]}